1
00:00:01,001 --> 00:00:03,128
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:11,052 --> 00:00:12,262
[Ivy] <i>Mom, are you here?</i>

3
00:00:12,345 --> 00:00:13,930
-[Camia screaming]
-[dishes break]

4
00:00:15,849 --> 00:00:17,100
<i>Mom!</i>

5
00:00:17,183 --> 00:00:18,309
<i>Mom?</i>

6
00:00:18,393 --> 00:00:19,310
<i>Mom…</i>

7
00:00:19,394 --> 00:00:21,980
<i>Can't you remember me? Or anything?</i>

8
00:00:22,063 --> 00:00:25,984
<i>What did they do to you, Mom?</i>
<i>What happened to you?</i>

9
00:00:26,776 --> 00:00:27,777
[Raul] <i>Love?</i>

10
00:00:28,445 --> 00:00:30,822
<i>Is there something you want to tell me?</i>

11
00:00:32,157 --> 00:00:34,784
[Diego] <i>I'm sure of it. That girl is Lily.</i>

12
00:00:34,868 --> 00:00:37,245
<i>If they don't want to tell me,</i>
<i>then I'll look into it myself.</i>

13
00:00:37,328 --> 00:00:41,041
<i>-Leave your pit and face me!</i>
<i>-Fine, I will.</i>

14
00:00:41,124 --> 00:00:42,959
<i>But I'm not a coward</i>
<i>because I'm not afraid of you.</i>

15
00:00:43,042 --> 00:00:46,671
<i>Tonight, all your lies</i>
<i>will come to an end.</i>

16
00:00:46,755 --> 00:00:49,966
[Ivy] <i>We have to leave before</i>
<i>that bastard returns.</i>

17
00:00:50,049 --> 00:00:52,343
<i>-He's kind! He's kind!</i>
<i>-We should leave.</i>

18
00:00:52,427 --> 00:00:55,555
<i>He is not kind! He's the reason</i>
<i>we became like this!</i>

19
00:00:55,638 --> 00:00:58,433
<i>Why our family fell apart! He is not kind!</i>

20
00:00:58,933 --> 00:01:00,977
<i>I won't let you hurt Grandpa again!</i>

21
00:01:01,061 --> 00:01:02,562
<i>I already know everything. They told me.</i>

22
00:01:02,645 --> 00:01:04,564
<i>I know what you traitors did!</i>

23
00:01:04,647 --> 00:01:09,277
<i>You are going to resign as</i>
<i>governor of Poblacion Ardiente.</i>

24
00:01:09,360 --> 00:01:11,946
<i>You can't do this, Papa.</i>
<i>You cannot do this!</i>

25
00:01:12,030 --> 00:01:14,741
<i>Kill Raul, and you can keep</i>
<i>your governorship.</i>

26
00:01:14,824 --> 00:01:17,702
<i>I will expose this family's</i>
<i>dirtiest secrets!</i>

27
00:01:17,786 --> 00:01:20,163
[scoffs] <i>Go! Go ahead, Raul.</i>

28
00:01:20,246 --> 00:01:23,583
<i>Give me one good reason</i>
<i>to finally get rid of you!</i>

29
00:01:23,666 --> 00:01:26,169
<i>I will kill you.</i>
<i>Get this trash out of here!</i>

30
00:01:26,252 --> 00:01:27,545
-[Raul] <i>Emilia!</i>
-[Emilia] <i>Please stop!</i>

31
00:01:27,629 --> 00:01:28,797
-[Raul] <i>Let go!</i>
-[Emilia] <i>Raul…</i>

32
00:01:28,880 --> 00:01:31,007
-[Raul] <i>I can't stay here!</i>
-[Emilia] <i>Just go with them.</i>

33
00:01:32,759 --> 00:01:37,222
[somber music playing]

34
00:01:42,644 --> 00:01:43,561
[door rattles]

35
00:01:53,321 --> 00:01:54,405
[thumping]

36
00:02:06,084 --> 00:02:11,005
[suspenseful music playing]

37
00:02:44,873 --> 00:02:46,207
[music fading]

38
00:02:46,875 --> 00:02:49,085
Aunt Claire, what are we going to do?

39
00:02:49,460 --> 00:02:51,462
I'm running out of options already.

40
00:02:52,672 --> 00:02:54,132
We will fight Julio head-on.

41
00:02:54,966 --> 00:02:56,009
How?!

42
00:02:56,634 --> 00:02:58,344
I will talk to some of my lawyer friends.

43
00:02:58,428 --> 00:03:00,889
I'm sure they'll find
a loophole in his plans.

44
00:03:02,348 --> 00:03:03,850
Are they ready to die?

45
00:03:04,100 --> 00:03:07,020
Because I'm sure they'll
be Papa's future targets.

46
00:03:08,813 --> 00:03:11,316
Raul, would you mind?
You're just standing there!

47
00:03:11,649 --> 00:03:14,110
Help us solve this problem!

48
00:03:14,819 --> 00:03:17,363
You know what?
Do whatever the hell you want.

49
00:03:17,947 --> 00:03:19,699
I don't give a crap.

50
00:03:19,782 --> 00:03:21,534
All I know is I have to get out of here.

51
00:03:21,951 --> 00:03:23,703
How dare you, Raul?!

52
00:03:24,245 --> 00:03:26,873
I chose you over being a governor,

53
00:03:26,956 --> 00:03:28,416
and this is what you're gonna do to me?

54
00:03:28,499 --> 00:03:29,417
How dare you!

55
00:03:29,500 --> 00:03:31,127
I should've done this a long time ago.

56
00:03:31,210 --> 00:03:32,587
I should've left you way back!

57
00:03:33,880 --> 00:03:35,548
So, if you'll excuse me, I have to leave.

58
00:03:35,632 --> 00:03:36,507
Don't you dare.

59
00:03:36,591 --> 00:03:37,592
-Hold on.
-Sir, you can't.

60
00:03:37,675 --> 00:03:38,635
[Emilia] Come on, try it.

61
00:03:38,718 --> 00:03:40,094
[bodyguard] Sir, please. You can't leave.

62
00:03:40,178 --> 00:03:42,680
Emilia, come on! Why are you doing this?

63
00:03:44,015 --> 00:03:45,141
[grunts] Ouch!

64
00:03:46,226 --> 00:03:47,018
[grunting]

65
00:03:47,101 --> 00:03:49,729
-Emilia, won't you stop them?
-[Emilia] No.

66
00:03:50,480 --> 00:03:54,609
Raul has to realize that I'm
the only one he's got left.

67
00:03:54,984 --> 00:03:56,069
[groans]

68
00:03:58,279 --> 00:04:01,741
[suspenseful music playing]

69
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:15,004
[instrumental theme music playing]

70
00:04:16,130 --> 00:04:17,131
[sighs]

71
00:04:37,318 --> 00:04:39,195
You haven't changed, Mom.

72
00:04:39,779 --> 00:04:41,281
You're still beautiful.

73
00:04:45,410 --> 00:04:50,665
When I was a kid, Mom, I told myself…

74
00:04:54,419 --> 00:04:55,628
I wish…

75
00:04:58,715 --> 00:05:00,967
I'd be as beautiful as my mother.

76
00:05:08,599 --> 00:05:10,977
I remember our life back then, Mom.

77
00:05:13,563 --> 00:05:18,943
<i>We didn't have much, but we were so happy.</i>

78
00:05:26,784 --> 00:05:27,910
[sighs]

79
00:05:31,748 --> 00:05:33,333
Mom, when I was a kid…

80
00:05:34,876 --> 00:05:36,127
do you know…

81
00:05:39,047 --> 00:05:41,966
what I really love that
you and Dad would always do?

82
00:05:42,508 --> 00:05:44,302
It was during bedtime…

83
00:05:47,180 --> 00:05:51,434
<i>when you and Dad would read</i>
<i>to me</i> The Count of Monte Cristo<i>.</i>

84
00:05:52,185 --> 00:05:54,228
<i>That was my favorite book, Mom.</i>

85
00:05:56,564 --> 00:05:58,775
I never imagined that…

86
00:06:01,486 --> 00:06:03,863
what happened in the book…

87
00:06:07,867 --> 00:06:08,868
would…

88
00:06:09,577 --> 00:06:13,206
would also happen to us?

89
00:06:14,457 --> 00:06:15,958
To our family.

90
00:06:22,715 --> 00:06:24,300
Thirteen years…

91
00:06:25,635 --> 00:06:28,054
[instrumental theme music
continues playing]

92
00:06:29,680 --> 00:06:31,557
I longed for you.

93
00:06:33,976 --> 00:06:35,311
And now, Mom?

94
00:06:39,232 --> 00:06:40,942
I'm with you again.

95
00:06:43,361 --> 00:06:44,570
But it hurts…

96
00:06:53,454 --> 00:06:54,580
[sniffles]

97
00:06:55,081 --> 00:06:58,042
It hurts because you can't remember me.

98
00:07:03,589 --> 00:07:07,260
It hurts because
you don't know me as Lily.

99
00:07:10,596 --> 00:07:13,182
You don't see me as your daughter.

100
00:07:19,564 --> 00:07:20,690
[sniffles]

101
00:07:26,946 --> 00:07:29,073
But I won't give up, Mom.

102
00:07:30,283 --> 00:07:32,160
I'll do everything…

103
00:07:34,704 --> 00:07:40,376
Everything I can to help you
regain your memories.

104
00:07:40,460 --> 00:07:44,464
["Wildflower" by Arnel Pineda playing]

105
00:07:46,340 --> 00:07:48,259
So you can recognize me again.

106
00:07:53,055 --> 00:07:54,390
I promise, Mom.

107
00:07:56,517 --> 00:08:00,480
["Wildflower" by Arnel Pineda
continues playing]

108
00:08:06,819 --> 00:08:08,529
[voice breaking] I love you, Mom.

109
00:08:12,200 --> 00:08:13,910
[song fading]

110
00:08:14,952 --> 00:08:16,162
Nanny, Uncle…

111
00:08:16,787 --> 00:08:18,956
I'll do everything to find out the truth.

112
00:08:19,040 --> 00:08:21,375
Diego, isn't it too dangerous?

113
00:08:21,459 --> 00:08:24,670
What if they won't let you in
at Miss Ivy's office in Manila?

114
00:08:25,338 --> 00:08:26,797
I'll find a way.

115
00:08:27,840 --> 00:08:29,342
Take care, Diego.

116
00:08:30,051 --> 00:08:31,928
You're getting in too deep.

117
00:08:33,221 --> 00:08:36,432
Don't worry about me. I know my limits.

118
00:08:37,266 --> 00:08:39,519
I just want answers to my questions.

119
00:08:40,645 --> 00:08:43,606
So I can freely love Ivy… or Lily.

120
00:08:46,400 --> 00:08:47,944
I'll get going now, Nanny, Uncle.

121
00:08:48,736 --> 00:08:50,530
-Take care!
-Be safe.

122
00:08:54,825 --> 00:08:56,118
[car engine starts]

123
00:09:08,881 --> 00:09:11,676
[sizzling]

124
00:09:22,270 --> 00:09:26,232
[ominous music playing]

125
00:10:00,266 --> 00:10:01,267
Mom.

126
00:10:04,770 --> 00:10:06,147
Good thing you're awake now.

127
00:10:07,064 --> 00:10:08,065
Uh…

128
00:10:08,774 --> 00:10:11,902
I'm just cooking fried rice.

129
00:10:16,407 --> 00:10:19,035
You used to cook this for me and Dad.

130
00:10:19,452 --> 00:10:22,747
Fried rice, corned beef, and eggs.

131
00:10:24,373 --> 00:10:27,251
Then we'd eat breakfast together.

132
00:10:28,753 --> 00:10:33,424
After breakfast, we'd leave
the house together too.

133
00:10:33,841 --> 00:10:35,718
Dad would go to his office,

134
00:10:35,801 --> 00:10:40,723
while you and I would head off to school.

135
00:10:42,767 --> 00:10:44,393
[Camia] <i>I'm Camia Cruz.</i>

136
00:10:44,477 --> 00:10:46,020
[teacher] <i>You teach Social Studies, right?</i>

137
00:10:46,103 --> 00:10:47,647
<i>Good afternoon, sir. I'm Camia Cruz.</i>

138
00:10:47,730 --> 00:10:48,856
<i>I tutor Diego.</i>

139
00:10:48,939 --> 00:10:51,567
<i>I said take your hands off me!</i>
<i>Don't touch me!</i>

140
00:10:51,984 --> 00:10:54,987
[tense music playing]

141
00:10:57,615 --> 00:10:58,616
Mom?

142
00:10:59,700 --> 00:11:01,952
Mom, does your head hurt again?

143
00:11:02,036 --> 00:11:04,580
[breathing heavily]

144
00:11:06,082 --> 00:11:07,166
Here.

145
00:11:07,708 --> 00:11:09,377
[water pouring]

146
00:11:10,002 --> 00:11:11,587
Drink this, Mom.

147
00:11:14,131 --> 00:11:15,466
-[glass breaks]
-[grunts]

148
00:11:17,760 --> 00:11:19,970
[Ivy groaning]

149
00:11:26,143 --> 00:11:27,561
[Ivy groaning]

150
00:11:28,938 --> 00:11:30,981
I'm okay, Mom.

151
00:11:31,065 --> 00:11:33,984
Move away, you might get hurt too.

152
00:11:37,279 --> 00:11:38,280
Come here.

153
00:11:40,866 --> 00:11:41,992
Come here.

154
00:11:42,827 --> 00:11:46,330
[instrumental theme music playing]

155
00:12:00,469 --> 00:12:01,720
Sit down.

156
00:12:01,804 --> 00:12:02,972
Wait a sec.

157
00:12:04,515 --> 00:12:07,977
[instrumental theme music playing]

158
00:12:12,606 --> 00:12:15,443
[Carlotta] Okay, I'll tell her
when she comes back,

159
00:12:15,526 --> 00:12:18,696
but call me if she drops
by the office, okay?

160
00:12:18,779 --> 00:12:20,448
-Yes, Miss Carlotta.
-Okay.

161
00:12:20,531 --> 00:12:21,574
I'll go now. Thank you.

162
00:12:21,657 --> 00:12:23,033
-Ma'am?
-Yes?

163
00:12:23,117 --> 00:12:24,535
Where's Ivy? I need to see her.

164
00:12:24,618 --> 00:12:28,539
Good morning, Mayor.
She left this morning.

165
00:12:28,622 --> 00:12:29,582
Where did she go?

166
00:12:29,665 --> 00:12:31,500
I assume she didn't go
to her office in Manila

167
00:12:31,584 --> 00:12:33,210
because her assistant is here.

168
00:12:33,294 --> 00:12:37,339
[nervous chuckle]
Joan got here after she left.

169
00:12:37,423 --> 00:12:38,507
Is that true?

170
00:12:38,591 --> 00:12:40,885
-Uh, yes, sir.
-Okay, call her now.

171
00:12:42,761 --> 00:12:44,346
-Ah…
-Come on, hurry up!

172
00:12:45,723 --> 00:12:47,558
[voice prompt] <i>The subscriber</i>
<i>cannot be reached.</i>

173
00:12:47,641 --> 00:12:49,310
<i>Please try again later.</i>

174
00:12:49,393 --> 00:12:50,853
[Arnaldo] Out of reach?

175
00:12:50,936 --> 00:12:53,272
I've been trying to contact her
since last night.

176
00:12:53,355 --> 00:12:55,399
Tell me where she went. Out with it.

177
00:12:55,483 --> 00:12:57,943
Mayor, I already answered you.

178
00:12:58,736 --> 00:13:02,198
And I think you need to leave.

179
00:13:02,281 --> 00:13:04,116
[voice shaking] You're trespassing.

180
00:13:04,200 --> 00:13:05,659
Trespassing?

181
00:13:07,411 --> 00:13:08,871
But I'm the mayor here.

182
00:13:10,915 --> 00:13:12,082
I know, sir.

183
00:13:13,250 --> 00:13:15,711
But that's exactly why you have to leave.

184
00:13:16,253 --> 00:13:19,548
I don't want to file a complaint.

185
00:13:19,632 --> 00:13:20,883
[chuckles sarcastically]

186
00:13:20,966 --> 00:13:22,426
[Arnaldo] She'll file a complaint.

187
00:13:22,510 --> 00:13:23,761
Did you hear that?

188
00:13:24,720 --> 00:13:25,846
[sighs]

189
00:13:27,348 --> 00:13:29,975
Carlotta, I know Ivy's hiding
something from me.

190
00:13:31,936 --> 00:13:33,854
And I swear, I'll find out what it is.

191
00:13:33,938 --> 00:13:37,441
[tense music playing]

192
00:13:48,202 --> 00:13:49,537
[sighs heavily]

193
00:14:07,096 --> 00:14:08,722
[inhales sharply, groans]

194
00:14:11,308 --> 00:14:12,309
Does it hurt?

195
00:14:17,314 --> 00:14:19,775
[soft music playing]

196
00:14:25,865 --> 00:14:28,325
[water pouring]

197
00:14:42,298 --> 00:14:43,299
Hang on.

198
00:15:12,161 --> 00:15:16,081
[soft music playing]

199
00:15:26,050 --> 00:15:27,051
[sniffles]

200
00:15:28,177 --> 00:15:29,136
Why?

201
00:15:31,430 --> 00:15:32,431
[sniffles]

202
00:15:33,724 --> 00:15:37,978
I just missed…
how you used to take care of me.

203
00:15:38,228 --> 00:15:39,313
[Ivy sniffles]

204
00:15:42,483 --> 00:15:45,444
[soft music playing]

205
00:15:56,163 --> 00:15:57,206
Let's eat.

206
00:15:59,416 --> 00:16:00,417
Okay, Mom.

207
00:16:02,378 --> 00:16:03,420
Take a seat, Mom.

208
00:16:11,261 --> 00:16:12,554
Thank you.

209
00:16:14,223 --> 00:16:18,143
[soft music playing]

210
00:16:47,423 --> 00:16:49,425
[foreboding music playing]

211
00:16:50,634 --> 00:16:51,844
Excuse me, sir?

212
00:16:53,012 --> 00:16:56,265
Uh… Good afternoon, miss.
Is this the Aguas Building?

213
00:16:56,348 --> 00:16:57,641
How can I help you, sir?

214
00:16:58,058 --> 00:17:00,352
I'm looking for Aguas Realty Department.

215
00:17:00,728 --> 00:17:02,146
Do you have an appointment, sir?

216
00:17:02,813 --> 00:17:03,814
Uh, no.

217
00:17:03,897 --> 00:17:06,483
But I just want to inquire
about the properties for sale.

218
00:17:06,984 --> 00:17:07,943
We can only entertain

219
00:17:08,027 --> 00:17:10,029
walk-in clients
through our marketing team.

220
00:17:10,112 --> 00:17:13,323
The stairs are to my left.
You can inquire downstairs.

221
00:17:13,949 --> 00:17:15,659
-Thank you.
-You're welcome, sir.

222
00:17:29,173 --> 00:17:31,967
Mom, you should eat some more.

223
00:17:32,051 --> 00:17:33,635
You only had a little.

224
00:17:36,346 --> 00:17:37,681
Are you full?

225
00:17:37,931 --> 00:17:39,600
All right, just drink this water.

226
00:17:53,322 --> 00:17:54,448
Come with me.

227
00:17:58,410 --> 00:17:59,620
Where to, Mom?

228
00:18:07,252 --> 00:18:08,212
Mom?

229
00:18:10,339 --> 00:18:11,507
You should sleep.

230
00:18:12,466 --> 00:18:13,801
Oh, no, I can't.

231
00:18:13,884 --> 00:18:16,428
Raul might come back. I can't sleep.

232
00:18:16,512 --> 00:18:18,597
You're tired. You should rest.

233
00:18:19,181 --> 00:18:21,058
-Mom, I'm okay.
-Lie down.

234
00:18:23,143 --> 00:18:24,186
But Mom…

235
00:18:32,027 --> 00:18:33,028
Mom--

236
00:18:34,822 --> 00:18:36,073
Go to sleep.

237
00:18:36,156 --> 00:18:40,160
[instrumental theme music playing]

238
00:18:48,085 --> 00:18:49,294
Thank you, Mom.

239
00:18:52,673 --> 00:18:59,638
["Wildflower" by Arnel Pineda playing]
<i>♪ Let her cry, for she's a lady ♪</i>

240
00:18:59,721 --> 00:19:03,100
<i>♪ Let her dream ♪</i>

241
00:19:03,183 --> 00:19:04,935
<i>♪ For she's a child ♪</i>

242
00:19:05,018 --> 00:19:06,270
<i>♪ She's a child ♪</i>

243
00:19:06,353 --> 00:19:10,357
<i>♪ Let the rain fall down ♪</i>

244
00:19:10,440 --> 00:19:13,819
<i>♪ Upon her ♪</i>

245
00:19:13,902 --> 00:19:17,531
<i>♪ She's a free and gentle flower ♪</i>

246
00:19:17,614 --> 00:19:20,868
<i>♪ Growing wild ♪</i>

247
00:19:20,951 --> 00:19:27,875
<i>♪ Let her cry, for she's a lady ♪</i>

248
00:19:27,958 --> 00:19:31,837
<i>♪ Let her dream ♪</i>

249
00:19:31,920 --> 00:19:33,755
<i>♪ She's a child ♪</i>

250
00:19:33,839 --> 00:19:35,507
[song fading]

251
00:19:36,717 --> 00:19:37,968
[sighs heavily]

252
00:19:39,136 --> 00:19:41,597
[tense music playing]

253
00:19:45,726 --> 00:19:46,977
Dad, we need to talk.

254
00:19:47,895 --> 00:19:49,605
Be honest. What's going on
between you and Ivy?

255
00:19:50,939 --> 00:19:51,857
Nothing.

256
00:19:51,940 --> 00:19:54,026
Then why did you both disappear
during my party?

257
00:19:54,151 --> 00:19:57,029
You too, Arnaldo?
Didn't we talk about this--

258
00:19:57,112 --> 00:20:00,782
I won't stop until you tell me
where you took Ivy.

259
00:20:01,158 --> 00:20:02,367
She's missing!

260
00:20:02,701 --> 00:20:04,369
I don't know what you're
talking about, Arnaldo.

261
00:20:04,453 --> 00:20:07,539
You don't? Dad, you can't deny
what kind of man you are.

262
00:20:09,082 --> 00:20:11,501
Did you kidnap her so you
could get back at Grandpa?

263
00:20:11,835 --> 00:20:14,129
So he won't touch you
after what you did to him?

264
00:20:14,213 --> 00:20:16,089
Don't test my patience, Arnaldo!

265
00:20:17,174 --> 00:20:18,884
And just so you know,

266
00:20:19,301 --> 00:20:22,763
your grandfather is just using that woman.

267
00:20:23,096 --> 00:20:24,765
Right now, she's useful to him.

268
00:20:24,848 --> 00:20:27,684
But sooner or later,
he'll get rid of her too.

269
00:20:28,560 --> 00:20:29,645
Just like you.

270
00:20:29,728 --> 00:20:32,439
That's how your grandfather
sees you and your mom!

271
00:20:33,023 --> 00:20:36,360
That's how wicked and selfish
your grandfather is!

272
00:20:37,027 --> 00:20:38,070
Wicked?

273
00:20:38,737 --> 00:20:41,156
Tough words from someone
who isn't a saint, Dad.

274
00:20:42,658 --> 00:20:48,330
Ever since I can remember, Grandpa has
been more like a father to me than you.

275
00:20:49,915 --> 00:20:53,919
[tense music playing]

276
00:21:13,939 --> 00:21:16,942
[suspenseful music playing]

277
00:21:40,215 --> 00:21:43,844
[no audio]

278
00:22:00,402 --> 00:22:02,195
I like that smile, Emilia.

279
00:22:03,613 --> 00:22:07,200
So, are you going with my suggestion

280
00:22:07,284 --> 00:22:09,286
to challenge Julio head-on?

281
00:22:10,912 --> 00:22:13,415
You said it yourself, Aunt Claire.

282
00:22:13,957 --> 00:22:16,001
I can't go down without a fight.

283
00:22:21,882 --> 00:22:24,009
[Claire] Humiliate Julio
in front of the media

284
00:22:24,092 --> 00:22:25,343
and the public.

285
00:22:26,803 --> 00:22:29,306
Show them the monster he really is.

286
00:22:29,389 --> 00:22:32,851
[sinister music playing]

287
00:22:42,360 --> 00:22:43,570
[exhales]

288
00:22:47,616 --> 00:22:49,451
Good day, Governor. This way, please.

289
00:22:49,951 --> 00:22:52,329
[Emilia] Hi. Hello there. Hi! Hello.

290
00:22:52,412 --> 00:22:53,705
Hi.

291
00:22:54,706 --> 00:22:56,458
Governor, this way, please.

292
00:23:03,507 --> 00:23:05,717
Good afternoon. Good afternoon.

293
00:23:06,176 --> 00:23:08,386
-Thank you for coming.
-[woman] Congressman!

294
00:23:09,596 --> 00:23:10,430
My dad is here.

295
00:23:10,514 --> 00:23:12,182
-Good day, sir.
-[Julio] Good day.

296
00:23:15,018 --> 00:23:16,269
[man] How are you?

297
00:23:17,229 --> 00:23:19,731
[Julio] How are you? Sit down, please.

298
00:23:20,649 --> 00:23:21,858
Hello.

299
00:23:21,942 --> 00:23:22,901
Hi.

300
00:23:25,320 --> 00:23:28,907
Raul, Claire, please join us.

301
00:23:30,408 --> 00:23:31,493
Come on.

302
00:23:32,160 --> 00:23:35,080
-[woman] This way, please.
-[Julio] Thank you, dear.

303
00:23:35,163 --> 00:23:36,081
You're welcome, sir.

304
00:23:36,164 --> 00:23:38,083
-Pa.
-Hello, Emilia.

305
00:23:40,794 --> 00:23:43,213
[tense music playing]

306
00:23:45,423 --> 00:23:48,593
-[reporter 1] Hello, sir.
-Hello. Good day to you all.

307
00:23:48,677 --> 00:23:51,304
[reporter 2] Thank you, sir,
for gracing us today.

308
00:23:51,388 --> 00:23:54,141
[Julio] We should be the ones
thanking you.

309
00:23:54,808 --> 00:23:56,518
Please, sit down. Sit down.

310
00:24:00,730 --> 00:24:02,566
Thank you. Thank you very much.

311
00:24:03,316 --> 00:24:04,359
Please.

312
00:24:06,695 --> 00:24:08,822
First of all,
to our friends from the press,

313
00:24:08,905 --> 00:24:10,824
thank you very much for coming.

314
00:24:11,700 --> 00:24:15,954
To my beloved children
of Poblacion Ardiente,

315
00:24:16,037 --> 00:24:19,624
with a warm smile, your Señor Julio,

316
00:24:20,458 --> 00:24:23,044
together with the rest
of the Ardiente Family,

317
00:24:23,128 --> 00:24:25,255
wishes to formally thank you,

318
00:24:25,338 --> 00:24:31,011
for your support and prayers
for my recovery.

319
00:24:32,512 --> 00:24:37,350
However, it's only fair that
with public service…

320
00:24:38,435 --> 00:24:41,438
comes fatigue and stress.

321
00:24:43,398 --> 00:24:46,943
To be honest, I really want
to be genuinely happy…

322
00:24:48,528 --> 00:24:49,696
but I just can't.

323
00:24:52,115 --> 00:24:54,951
Because there's another crisis…

324
00:24:55,619 --> 00:24:59,456
threatening the Ardiente family.

325
00:25:01,875 --> 00:25:04,211
And as your humble servants…

326
00:25:05,921 --> 00:25:09,049
we feel that we should let you know…

327
00:25:09,966 --> 00:25:10,967
[camera shutter clicks]

328
00:25:15,722 --> 00:25:17,265
that my daughter, Emilia…

329
00:25:18,308 --> 00:25:19,309
[Julio sniffles]

330
00:25:20,560 --> 00:25:24,940
She has been diagnosed
with ovarian cancer, stage 2.

331
00:25:30,612 --> 00:25:34,407
[no audible dialogue]

332
00:25:38,495 --> 00:25:39,454
[camera shutter clicks]

333
00:25:42,207 --> 00:25:43,208
[camera shutter clicks]

334
00:25:43,375 --> 00:25:45,502
Our family has already
discussed the matter.

335
00:25:47,087 --> 00:25:50,215
Emilia's health
is of the utmost importance.

336
00:25:52,509 --> 00:25:56,888
So, today, there is something
she would like to announce.

337
00:26:00,976 --> 00:26:02,686
Hello, friends. [chuckles nervously]

338
00:26:03,019 --> 00:26:04,062
[Emilia] Ah…

339
00:26:04,646 --> 00:26:07,732
You know how much I love you all.

340
00:26:08,066 --> 00:26:10,110
Especially my constituents.

341
00:26:10,318 --> 00:26:15,198
But we all face challenges
at some point in our lives.

342
00:26:15,907 --> 00:26:20,370
And right now, I am dealing
with a health crisis…

343
00:26:21,246 --> 00:26:24,082
as my father has just mentioned.

344
00:26:24,416 --> 00:26:25,750
And because of this…

345
00:26:26,418 --> 00:26:31,589
I would need to step down as
the governor of this province.

346
00:26:32,799 --> 00:26:34,342
But please don't worry.

347
00:26:34,801 --> 00:26:37,887
Because you know me, I'm a fighter.

348
00:26:38,680 --> 00:26:40,807
I'll fight this disease.

349
00:26:41,099 --> 00:26:44,853
So, when I come back,
I can serve you all once again.

350
00:26:45,186 --> 00:26:49,941
As a stronger and firmer leader
than before.

351
00:26:50,608 --> 00:26:53,320
So thank you very much.

352
00:26:54,029 --> 00:26:56,990
Your friend Emilia
loves you all very much.

353
00:26:57,073 --> 00:26:59,826
I love you all. I love you.
Thank you so much.

354
00:27:00,368 --> 00:27:03,038
-[camera shutter clicks]
-[applauding]

355
00:27:12,547 --> 00:27:14,007
Moving forward…

356
00:27:14,966 --> 00:27:19,387
we know that a lot of people
depend on the governor.

357
00:27:20,638 --> 00:27:24,392
So, the provincial council
has agreed that,

358
00:27:24,809 --> 00:27:29,522
in order for us to continue
our service to the public,

359
00:27:30,482 --> 00:27:33,651
the vice governor
will assume the vacant post.

360
00:27:34,986 --> 00:27:36,196
Please call the vice governor.

361
00:27:37,947 --> 00:27:39,908
Ladies and gentlemen of the press,

362
00:27:40,241 --> 00:27:43,787
my beloved children of Poblacion Ardiente,

363
00:27:43,995 --> 00:27:46,289
your Señor Julio would like to introduce

364
00:27:46,581 --> 00:27:49,125
one of his dearest friends in politics,

365
00:27:49,542 --> 00:27:52,420
Governor Emilia's successor,

366
00:27:53,171 --> 00:27:56,466
Governor William Alvarez!

367
00:27:57,425 --> 00:28:00,387
[all applauding]

368
00:28:06,768 --> 00:28:09,020
-Auntie, let's go?
-Okay.

369
00:28:11,189 --> 00:28:12,982
-We'll go ahead, Papa.
-Okay.

370
00:28:13,066 --> 00:28:15,485
-[Emilia] Bye, Governor.
-Okay, Emilia. Take care.

371
00:28:16,486 --> 00:28:18,113
-Emilia.
-Bye, Governor.

372
00:28:18,196 --> 00:28:20,323
Claire. Raul. Have a safe trip.

373
00:28:23,410 --> 00:28:24,411
Well…

374
00:28:25,995 --> 00:28:27,664
Here's to you, Governor.

375
00:28:28,331 --> 00:28:30,166
-Thank you, Congressman.
-[glasses clink]

376
00:28:30,667 --> 00:28:32,293
[Julio] Mayor, join us.

377
00:28:35,088 --> 00:28:40,927
You know, Arnaldo, our new
governor is a very good soldier.

378
00:28:41,845 --> 00:28:44,389
Reliable and loyal.

379
00:28:45,098 --> 00:28:46,349
Isn't that right, Alvarez?

380
00:28:46,850 --> 00:28:48,643
You can count on me, Congressman.

381
00:28:50,812 --> 00:28:54,733
When the time comes that
you step into my shoes,

382
00:28:55,358 --> 00:28:59,821
you'd want to be surrounded by
the likes of Governor Alvarez.

383
00:29:04,159 --> 00:29:05,285
I'll remember that, Grandpa.

384
00:29:05,577 --> 00:29:09,414
Well then, it seems
we are all in agreement.

385
00:29:10,665 --> 00:29:11,750
Viva Ardiente.

386
00:29:12,459 --> 00:29:14,461
-Viva Ardiente.
-Viva Ardiente.

387
00:29:14,544 --> 00:29:15,545
[glasses clink]

388
00:29:15,962 --> 00:29:17,589
Please excuse me for a while.

389
00:29:21,176 --> 00:29:25,180
[tense music playing]

390
00:29:28,349 --> 00:29:29,893
[William] What's our agenda for today?

391
00:29:36,649 --> 00:29:37,942
-Thank you.
-Sure, Governor.

392
00:29:39,068 --> 00:29:42,030
Excuse me, Congressman. I have to go.

393
00:29:42,739 --> 00:29:43,656
[Julio] Governor.

394
00:29:43,990 --> 00:29:46,451
Thank you very much for this
wonderful press conference.

395
00:29:46,534 --> 00:29:49,120
Thank you very much
for accepting the position.

396
00:29:49,245 --> 00:29:50,663
My honor and my pleasure.

397
00:29:51,915 --> 00:29:52,916
[Julio] Okay.

398
00:29:54,709 --> 00:29:56,294
-Arnaldo.
-Governor.

399
00:29:57,337 --> 00:29:58,588
I'll be seeing you.

400
00:29:59,464 --> 00:30:00,465
You will.

401
00:30:02,091 --> 00:30:03,426
Take care, Governor.

402
00:30:03,510 --> 00:30:04,719
You too, Congressman.

403
00:30:08,681 --> 00:30:11,684
[tense music playing]

404
00:30:13,978 --> 00:30:15,104
[Julio] I gathered you all here

405
00:30:15,188 --> 00:30:17,690
because I have an important task for you.

406
00:30:19,526 --> 00:30:24,280
I want you to take all the
belongings of Emilia and Raul…

407
00:30:25,490 --> 00:30:29,035
and move them to the old
guesthouse behind the house.

408
00:30:30,662 --> 00:30:33,331
Don't forget to move
Claire's belongings too.

409
00:30:34,207 --> 00:30:40,505
Now, if Emilia complains,
tell me immediately.

410
00:30:40,672 --> 00:30:43,591
I'll be the one to deal with her
accordingly.

411
00:30:44,551 --> 00:30:45,635
Is that clear?

412
00:30:46,177 --> 00:30:47,428
[all] Yes, Congressman.

413
00:30:47,804 --> 00:30:49,722
Good, you may all leave now.

414
00:30:53,935 --> 00:30:55,687
[sighs] Grandpa…

415
00:30:58,731 --> 00:30:59,941
Isn't that too much?

416
00:31:00,567 --> 00:31:02,819
I mean, you already got what you wanted.

417
00:31:03,236 --> 00:31:04,988
Mom stepped down from office.

418
00:31:06,364 --> 00:31:07,532
A little mercy?

419
00:31:07,866 --> 00:31:08,950
[scoffs]

420
00:31:09,951 --> 00:31:12,495
You know, Arnaldo, you don't understand.

421
00:31:12,579 --> 00:31:14,622
Your mom has to learn a lesson.

422
00:31:14,706 --> 00:31:19,752
And tapping her on the hand isn't enough.

423
00:31:21,337 --> 00:31:25,925
You need to cripple her for her to learn.

424
00:31:27,385 --> 00:31:30,305
Don't worry. Leave your mom to me.

425
00:31:30,388 --> 00:31:33,099
Leave this matter to me. Mark my words.

426
00:31:33,725 --> 00:31:37,020
The day will come when your
mother will thank me for this.

427
00:31:37,604 --> 00:31:38,521
[clicks tongue]

428
00:31:38,605 --> 00:31:43,359
In the meantime, I want you
to keep an eye on Miss Aguas.

429
00:31:45,361 --> 00:31:47,655
Find out where that woman went.

430
00:31:50,658 --> 00:31:51,784
Yes, Grandpa.

431
00:31:58,666 --> 00:31:59,792
[woman] Have a seat.

432
00:31:59,876 --> 00:32:01,002
[Diego] Thank you, ma'am.

433
00:32:02,045 --> 00:32:04,255
What's this interview for exactly?

434
00:32:05,548 --> 00:32:08,718
For a magazine feature
on Miss Ivy Aguas, ma'am.

435
00:32:09,344 --> 00:32:10,553
Hold on.

436
00:32:12,722 --> 00:32:13,890
[woman] Ivy?

437
00:32:13,973 --> 00:32:16,434
You mean the daughter
of Mrs. Prianka Aguas?

438
00:32:16,517 --> 00:32:19,270
Of course, I know her very well.

439
00:32:19,771 --> 00:32:21,105
She was a transferee,

440
00:32:21,189 --> 00:32:25,485
but we don't have any records
of her from her previous school.

441
00:32:25,610 --> 00:32:28,279
What do you want to know about Ivy?

442
00:32:29,781 --> 00:32:32,784
How was she as a student?

443
00:32:33,284 --> 00:32:34,827
A quiet one.

444
00:32:35,161 --> 00:32:37,372
She seldom talked to others.

445
00:32:37,455 --> 00:32:40,375
At times, she would just
stare off into space,

446
00:32:41,292 --> 00:32:43,211
especially during her first year here.

447
00:32:43,294 --> 00:32:47,507
According to Mrs. Aguas,
Ivy went through a lot.

448
00:32:48,675 --> 00:32:50,551
What do you mean, ma'am?

449
00:32:50,635 --> 00:32:53,888
It had something to do with her
childhood and her real mom.

450
00:32:54,514 --> 00:32:56,849
Apparently, it was something terrible.

451
00:32:58,893 --> 00:33:01,938
Hold on… Her real mom?

452
00:33:02,146 --> 00:33:05,233
Yes. Ivy is Mrs. Aguas' adopted daughter.

453
00:33:06,150 --> 00:33:10,154
But despite how hard it was for her,

454
00:33:10,238 --> 00:33:11,572
she was able to overcome it.

455
00:33:11,739 --> 00:33:15,994
She turned out to be a bright,
diligent, and kind student.

456
00:33:16,244 --> 00:33:20,456
No wonder Mrs. Aguas loved
and treated Ivy as her own.

457
00:33:20,915 --> 00:33:22,667
She graduated at the top of her class,

458
00:33:22,750 --> 00:33:24,919
both in grade school and high school.

459
00:33:25,086 --> 00:33:27,088
In fact, she's one of the most
outstanding students

460
00:33:27,171 --> 00:33:28,339
this school has produced.

461
00:33:28,631 --> 00:33:31,175
Would you like to see our Hall of Fame?

462
00:33:31,342 --> 00:33:35,096
You'll see Ivy's pictures
and achievements there.

463
00:33:35,471 --> 00:33:37,473
[tense music playing]

464
00:33:39,350 --> 00:33:40,101
[Emilia sniffles]

465
00:33:40,184 --> 00:33:43,896
Pull yourself together, Emilia.
You can't be like this!

466
00:33:45,273 --> 00:33:50,611
Auntie, I can't be anyone
or anything anymore!

467
00:33:50,903 --> 00:33:55,158
I'm nobody! I am nobody, Aunt Claire.

468
00:33:56,117 --> 00:33:59,037
Papa took away everything from me.

469
00:34:00,413 --> 00:34:02,665
He already found someone
to replace me as governor.

470
00:34:03,833 --> 00:34:07,170
Someone more capable and smarter.

471
00:34:07,253 --> 00:34:08,337
I don't know!

472
00:34:08,963 --> 00:34:11,799
[sobbing]

473
00:34:12,717 --> 00:34:14,427
[sighs] Emilia…

474
00:34:15,219 --> 00:34:18,931
You know, Aunt Claire,
sometimes, I wonder…

475
00:34:21,851 --> 00:34:24,145
Does Papa love me at all?

476
00:34:26,898 --> 00:34:27,899
[Emilia sniffles]

477
00:34:31,319 --> 00:34:33,946
Emilia, that's enough.

478
00:34:35,239 --> 00:34:36,407
[Claire] You've had enough!

479
00:34:38,701 --> 00:34:41,496
What are you all doing here?

480
00:34:42,038 --> 00:34:45,625
Hey! What's this about?
What are you doing here?

481
00:34:45,708 --> 00:34:48,711
Ma'am, Congressman ordered us
to transfer your things

482
00:34:48,795 --> 00:34:51,380
because you'll be moving
to the old guesthouse.

483
00:34:51,464 --> 00:34:55,593
No, no! Wait! Wait!
Don't you dare touch my stuff!

484
00:34:55,676 --> 00:34:57,386
-Hey, wait!
-Wait!

485
00:34:57,970 --> 00:34:59,972
Stay away from me!

486
00:35:01,349 --> 00:35:02,934
What are you doing?!

487
00:35:03,017 --> 00:35:05,478
Those are mine! Don't touch those!

488
00:35:05,561 --> 00:35:08,064
Wait! Those are my clothes! Give me that!

489
00:35:08,147 --> 00:35:09,315
-We're sorry, ma'am.
-Give it to me!

490
00:35:09,398 --> 00:35:11,442
-It's the congressman's orders.
-Don't you dare touch me!

491
00:35:11,526 --> 00:35:13,027
Don't you dare touch me!

492
00:35:13,152 --> 00:35:14,904
Hold on! Wait!

493
00:35:14,987 --> 00:35:16,864
-Those are my clothes!
-We're sorry, ma'am.

494
00:35:16,948 --> 00:35:18,074
We're just following orders.

495
00:35:18,157 --> 00:35:21,077
[Emilia] Those are mine!
Hey! That's expensive!

496
00:35:21,160 --> 00:35:23,621
-Give me that!
-We're really sorry, ma'am.

497
00:35:25,498 --> 00:35:28,626
Sorry?! What sorry?! You can't do this!

498
00:35:29,919 --> 00:35:31,420
This is not happening!

499
00:35:34,173 --> 00:35:37,844
[sobbing]

500
00:35:37,927 --> 00:35:39,095
Aunt Claire…

501
00:35:39,178 --> 00:35:40,638
[mouthing silently]

502
00:35:40,721 --> 00:35:42,181
[crying]

503
00:35:47,186 --> 00:35:48,312
[sighs heavily]

504
00:35:50,148 --> 00:35:52,942
Are you okay? Why do you look nervous?

505
00:35:54,902 --> 00:35:57,530
I'm just excited to know more
about Miss Aguas.

506
00:36:02,034 --> 00:36:03,202
Is this it?

507
00:36:04,954 --> 00:36:05,997
I'm sorry.

508
00:36:06,914 --> 00:36:08,416
My eyes aren't as good as they used to be.

509
00:36:08,499 --> 00:36:11,002
So, I can't recognize all the photos here.

510
00:36:12,253 --> 00:36:13,296
It's okay, ma'am.

511
00:36:24,015 --> 00:36:26,976
[tense music playing]

512
00:36:34,775 --> 00:36:36,235
[suspenseful sting]

513
00:36:39,739 --> 00:36:40,990
Is this Ivy?

514
00:36:44,827 --> 00:36:46,579
Yes, that's her.

515
00:36:51,250 --> 00:36:54,170
[suspenseful music playing]

516
00:36:56,005 --> 00:36:57,632
I have to go now.

517
00:36:59,592 --> 00:37:00,676
Thank you, ma'am.

518
00:37:04,055 --> 00:37:07,558
[suspenseful music playing]

519
00:37:18,778 --> 00:37:19,779
[camera shutter clicks]

520
00:37:28,120 --> 00:37:30,122
[Jepoy] You were right to call
your dad out, Mayor.

521
00:37:31,207 --> 00:37:33,542
I know I'm not in the position to talk,

522
00:37:34,585 --> 00:37:36,545
but in my one year of working here,

523
00:37:36,629 --> 00:37:40,049
I've seen that it's only Governor Emilia
and Congressman Julio

524
00:37:40,132 --> 00:37:41,592
who really love you.

525
00:37:45,513 --> 00:37:47,181
But I feel sorry for Governor Emilia

526
00:37:48,140 --> 00:37:49,892
considering what Sir Raul
was doing to her.

527
00:37:49,976 --> 00:37:51,727
If I were in your shoes, Mayor,

528
00:37:51,811 --> 00:37:55,022
if I were his son, I don't know
what I would have done to him.

529
00:37:57,817 --> 00:37:59,318
He's a pathetic bastard.

530
00:38:01,153 --> 00:38:02,822
And a worthless father.

531
00:38:06,867 --> 00:38:08,327
I just thought, Mayor…

532
00:38:08,953 --> 00:38:11,622
if Sir Raul could hurt your grandfather…

533
00:38:13,582 --> 00:38:15,710
how much more your mother?

534
00:38:18,337 --> 00:38:19,505
What do you mean?

535
00:38:20,631 --> 00:38:23,384
You need someone to protect
Governor Emilia from Sir Raul.

536
00:38:23,801 --> 00:38:24,927
Mayor…

537
00:38:25,845 --> 00:38:29,265
I volunteer myself to be
your mom's personal bodyguard.

538
00:38:32,143 --> 00:38:33,102
All right.

539
00:38:34,645 --> 00:38:36,314
But not just Mama's bodyguard.

540
00:38:37,690 --> 00:38:39,567
I also want you to watch over my dad.

541
00:38:40,484 --> 00:38:43,362
I want to know everything he does.

542
00:38:44,447 --> 00:38:45,781
As you wish, Mayor.

543
00:38:46,365 --> 00:38:47,366
[sighs]

544
00:38:53,539 --> 00:38:56,500
[somber music playing]

545
00:39:07,845 --> 00:39:09,638
<i>Miss! Miss, wait!</i>

546
00:39:09,889 --> 00:39:12,516
-<i>Yes?</i>
-[stuttering] <i>For you.</i>

547
00:39:14,060 --> 00:39:17,146
<i>-I'm Diego.</i>
<i>-Ivy Aguas.</i>

548
00:39:18,898 --> 00:39:19,774
<i>Miss Aguas.</i>

549
00:39:19,857 --> 00:39:23,652
<i>How will you benefit</i>
<i>from investing in Ardiente?</i>

550
00:39:27,656 --> 00:39:31,118
[woman] <i>According to Mrs. Aguas,</i>
<i>Ivy went through a lot.</i>

551
00:39:31,285 --> 00:39:34,330
<i>It had something to do with</i>
<i>her childhood and her real mom.</i>

552
00:39:34,413 --> 00:39:36,415
<i>-Her real mom?</i>
<i>-Yes.</i>

553
00:39:36,582 --> 00:39:38,709
<i>Ivy is Mrs. Aguas' adopted daughter.</i>

554
00:39:39,126 --> 00:39:42,797
<i>-Is this Ivy?</i>
<i>-Yes, that's her.</i>

555
00:39:48,636 --> 00:39:51,138
[young Diego] <i>What? Your family's leaving?</i>

556
00:39:51,222 --> 00:39:53,641
<i>If I leave, who's going to be your friend?</i>

557
00:39:53,724 --> 00:39:55,476
<i>No one will make me happy anymore.</i>

558
00:39:55,559 --> 00:39:58,938
<i>And if you leave, I'll be lonely again.</i>

559
00:39:59,939 --> 00:40:01,232
<i>I'll miss you.</i>

560
00:40:06,320 --> 00:40:08,781
<i>Lily, why did you have to lie to us?</i>

561
00:40:09,156 --> 00:40:11,075
<i>Why did you come back to Ardiente?</i>

562
00:40:11,158 --> 00:40:12,952
<i>And what suffering did you go through?</i>

563
00:40:13,035 --> 00:40:14,912
<i>What happened to your mom?</i>

564
00:40:25,464 --> 00:40:28,426
I'll ask you all about this
when I see you.

565
00:40:28,592 --> 00:40:32,179
I hope you'll finally tell me the truth.

566
00:40:39,145 --> 00:40:42,148
[somber music playing]

567
00:40:54,368 --> 00:40:55,411
[groans]

568
00:40:55,703 --> 00:40:58,497
I hate this house! It's too small!

569
00:40:59,248 --> 00:41:01,167
I don't want to live in this hellhole!

570
00:41:02,710 --> 00:41:06,589
Mark my words,
I'll return to that mansion!

571
00:41:06,672 --> 00:41:08,507
Mark my words!

572
00:41:10,551 --> 00:41:11,677
My shoes!

573
00:41:13,471 --> 00:41:14,889
I hate this!

574
00:41:14,972 --> 00:41:15,931
[exhales]

575
00:41:17,808 --> 00:41:21,228
[somber music playing]

576
00:41:24,231 --> 00:41:25,524
[house help] Good evening, sir.

577
00:41:25,941 --> 00:41:26,901
Ma'am.

578
00:41:26,984 --> 00:41:27,985
[Carlotta] Yes?

579
00:41:28,068 --> 00:41:29,236
Diego.

580
00:41:29,320 --> 00:41:32,072
Miss Carlotta, good evening.
Can I talk to Ivy?

581
00:41:32,156 --> 00:41:34,116
I'm afraid she isn't here.

582
00:41:35,534 --> 00:41:36,785
Where did she go?

583
00:41:36,869 --> 00:41:39,997
I don't know. I couldn't reach her either.

584
00:41:40,289 --> 00:41:44,835
Miss Carlotta, I'm begging you.
Please, let me talk to Ivy.

585
00:41:45,377 --> 00:41:47,546
About what, Diego?

586
00:41:49,173 --> 00:41:51,091
Ivy's been keeping a secret from me.

587
00:41:51,759 --> 00:41:53,427
-Secret?
-Ms. Carlotta, what do you know?

588
00:41:53,511 --> 00:41:55,721
What do you know about Ivy and Lily?

589
00:41:55,804 --> 00:41:57,223
[suspenseful music plays]

590
00:41:57,932 --> 00:41:58,891
Lily?

591
00:41:59,975 --> 00:42:01,894
I-- I don't know. Who's Lily?

592
00:42:01,977 --> 00:42:04,188
What are you talking about,
Diego? Just leave.

593
00:42:04,271 --> 00:42:05,564
-Miss Carlotta, please…
-You should leave.

594
00:42:05,648 --> 00:42:07,650
I have other matters to attend to, okay?

595
00:42:07,733 --> 00:42:09,818
[Diego] You don't have to lie anymore.

596
00:42:12,196 --> 00:42:14,573
I already know who Ivy really is.

597
00:42:14,657 --> 00:42:17,159
[tense music playing]

598
00:42:20,579 --> 00:42:23,541
I'll go now, Miss Carlotta. Thank you.

599
00:42:29,880 --> 00:42:31,048
[exhales]

600
00:42:36,387 --> 00:42:40,307
[foreboding music playing]

601
00:42:50,067 --> 00:42:52,069
[Ivy] <i>Mom, it's me.</i>

602
00:42:52,278 --> 00:42:53,946
<i>Mom, it's me, your daughter.</i>

603
00:42:55,656 --> 00:42:57,491
<i>Mom, it's me, Lily.</i>

604
00:42:59,702 --> 00:43:00,744
[Camia] <i>Lily?!</i>

605
00:43:01,787 --> 00:43:02,830
<i>Dear!</i>

606
00:43:03,455 --> 00:43:04,498
[Dante] <i>Lily?</i>

607
00:43:05,249 --> 00:43:06,250
[young Lily] <i>Mom?</i>

608
00:43:06,834 --> 00:43:07,835
<i>Mom?</i>

609
00:43:10,629 --> 00:43:13,632
[suspenseful music playing]

610
00:43:30,524 --> 00:43:32,359
[Dante] <i>Lily, are you all right there?</i>

611
00:43:32,443 --> 00:43:35,904
[Lily] <i>I'm fine, Dad.</i>
<i>This place looks great!</i>

612
00:43:35,988 --> 00:43:39,074
[suspenseful music playing]

613
00:43:44,913 --> 00:43:47,249
[suspenseful music continues playing]

614
00:43:49,001 --> 00:43:52,212
[breathing heavily]

615
00:43:52,296 --> 00:43:54,548
<i>-Mom? What happened to you?</i>
<i>-Lily, run…</i>

616
00:43:54,632 --> 00:43:55,841
-<i>Shush!</i>
-[Tonio] <i>Hey!</i>

617
00:43:56,425 --> 00:43:58,844
<i>Lily… Run!</i>

618
00:43:58,927 --> 00:44:00,137
[Lily] <i>Mom!</i>

619
00:44:01,680 --> 00:44:06,143
[breathing heavily]

620
00:44:07,728 --> 00:44:09,021
[voice shaking] Lily…

621
00:44:11,231 --> 00:44:13,067
Lily…

622
00:44:13,567 --> 00:44:14,985
Lily! [sobs]

623
00:44:16,070 --> 00:44:17,821
[sobbing] Lily!

624
00:44:18,405 --> 00:44:19,948
-Lily…
-Mom?

625
00:44:20,324 --> 00:44:21,992
-Mom?
-Lily…

626
00:44:22,493 --> 00:44:24,453
Lily…

627
00:44:24,536 --> 00:44:28,165
Yes, Mom, that's me.
Do you remember me now?

628
00:44:28,248 --> 00:44:31,752
-[sobbing]
-Do you remember me, Mom?

629
00:44:31,835 --> 00:44:34,630
Do you remember me now?
Yes, it's me. I'm Lily!

630
00:44:34,713 --> 00:44:36,715
[Camia sobbing]

631
00:44:37,341 --> 00:44:40,427
["Wildflower" by Arnel Pineda playing]
<i>♪ Let the rain ♪</i>

632
00:44:40,511 --> 00:44:45,516
<i>♪ Fall down upon her ♪</i>

633
00:44:45,599 --> 00:44:52,606
<i>♪ She's a free and gentle flower</i>
<i>Growing wild ♪</i>

634
00:44:52,689 --> 00:44:55,275
<i>♪ Let her cry ♪</i>

635
00:44:55,359 --> 00:44:59,738
<i>♪ For she's a lady ♪</i>

636
00:44:59,822 --> 00:45:03,117
<i>♪ Let her dream… ♪</i>

637
00:45:03,200 --> 00:45:05,911
<i>I won't rest until I've spoken to Ivy.</i>

638
00:45:05,994 --> 00:45:08,122
<i>I want to hear the truth</i>
<i>straight from her.</i>

639
00:45:08,205 --> 00:45:11,250
[Loring] <i>I think she's up to</i>
<i>something against your family.</i>

640
00:45:11,333 --> 00:45:13,544
<i>Why would I look for Ivy?</i>
<i>I don't need anything from her.</i>

641
00:45:13,627 --> 00:45:16,171
[Arnaldo] <i>Be sure of that. If I</i>
<i>learn you're betraying us again,</i>

642
00:45:16,255 --> 00:45:17,631
<i>I'll forget you're my brother.</i>

643
00:45:17,714 --> 00:45:20,467
<i>Right now, we only have each other.</i>

644
00:45:20,551 --> 00:45:21,718
<i>Just you and me.</i>

645
00:45:21,802 --> 00:45:25,764
<i>Where is Miss Aguas,</i>
<i>and what do you know about her?</i>

646
00:45:25,848 --> 00:45:26,974
<i>Answer me!</i>

647
00:45:27,057 --> 00:45:28,767
[Emilia] <i>You're going</i>
<i>to your mistress again?</i>

648
00:45:28,851 --> 00:45:30,853
<i>Go on, do it. I'll burn her to ashes!</i>

649
00:45:33,355 --> 00:45:36,024
<i>Good job. </i>[laughing maniacally]

650
00:45:36,108 --> 00:45:39,153
[theme music playing]
